   "**An alliance held together by a common enemy tells you nothing about what it will do when the enemy is gone** — the effect of the Ethiopian Peoples' Forces Alliance for Survival — Tigrayan forces now fighting beside the Fano movement and the Oromo Liberation Army, groups that fought against them four years ago — is that its members share a target and not a programme; the compound consequence is that the war's political end-state is undefined even to its victors, so any ceasefire reached with this coalition will be a ceasefire between parties who have not agreed on what Ethiopia should be — the exact defect of the 2022 Pretoria settlement, repeating",
