  "verse": "Truly, you have already created a world-judgement in the form of immense catastrophes which break in over you and which you already can no longer evade; you are in the midst of a self-created tremendous storm which is brewing over you and which now pours out terribleness and destruction over you, and if you continue to potter about as before, then the elimination is going to break in over you without hope of rescue; therefore you shall bethink yourselves and search for the way of the truth in order to walk upon it and to follow the creational laws and recommendations, because only by doing so can you still prevent the worst.",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 28, Verse 160",
  "hinge": "The cause is not the El Niño — that is weather, and weather is not a moral agent. The cause is the choice to burn one of the world's largest peatland systems for cheap land, in a season whose severity was forecast, and to answer a measured health emergency with water-bombing and advisories rather than with the enforcement and the distributed protection that would reduce the cases inside the six weeks that remain. §160 does not describe the storm as punitive; it describes it as **self-created**, and it names the only exit — *\"bethink yourselves… because only by doing so can you still prevent the worst.\"* Note the tense: *still*. The environment minister has said what is coming and roughly when it ends. Indonesia, Malaysia and Singapore hold between them the authority over the fires, the funds for the suppression, and the population that will breathe the result. Strengthened enforcement on peat, suppression funded as a shared regional cost, and protection distributed to the 12.5 million rather than advised at them: each is a decision available this week. The temperature is not negotiated. The case count inside it is."
